ll in hotels because the government  hasn't sorted their situation out and  that they arrived last August so that's  just a terrible letdown of people again  who are vulnerable and fled persecution  and then ministers have added a three to  six month delay and added bureaucracy  into the Asylum decision making process  well of course that means you've then  got more people waiting in Asylum  accommodation where would you put them  this is the thing where well if you make  dinner to decide their claims because  then for those who are refugees  literally they can then work they can  then get on with their lives they can  get the support that they need if you've  made the decision if they're not  refugees they of course need to be  returned so it's that failure to make  decisions which means we've now got so  many more people waiting in Asylum  accommodation who are waiting for  decisions to be made and that's why you  then also end up with this overcrowding  at manston because there isn't anywhere  to move people to so at the heart of  this is the conservatives failure to  actually make the system work to just  take basic decisions in a fair and  sensible way and also to fail to work  with France on how you prevent the  dangerous Boat Crossings in the first  place does the labor party have a policy  on the numbers of people that he thinks  will be acceptable to be coming to the  country per year do you mean refugees or  do you mean the overall the overall so  so we think that you should have this  points-based system where you look at  different kinds of immigration rather  than having the kind of targets where  there's a bit of a row going on at the  moment in the government between some  parts of the government who seem to want  a net migration Target which goes back  to the old Cameron one which didn't work  of much a lower Target others who seem  to want actually a much higher overall  Target because they think it will  improve growth we don't think either of  tho